SUMMARY:2nd Update: Walking the Forest Meadow at the NC Arboretum
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\n**2nd Update: The Bonsai 
 in the Blue Ridge ticketed event will be going on June 4 – 7. Admission 
 to the indoor exhibit area is $5. You very well may want to stay after the
  walk for lunch and the Bonsai event. Plan accordingly.**\n\nMeet inside t
 he Baker Visitor Center at 09:30 a.m. Restrooms are available at the start
  point.\n\nWe will walk through the Formal Gardens and the Bonsai Exhibit.
  Then we will make our way to the Forest Meadow\, walking around all the p
 aths. We'll go down Running Cedar Road\, across on Bent Creek Road (taking
  the Creekside Trails)\, and return on **Wolf Branch** Road.\n\nDress for 
 the weather\; consider a hat and sunscreen. Some may want walking poles. S
 neakers should be fine\, unless it has rained recently. Be sure to bring p
 lenty of water and a protein snack.\n\nDogs on leash are welcome but are n
 ot allowed in buildings or the Bonsai Exhibit. Trail strollers should be o
 k.\n\nThe NC Arboretum does not have an admission fee\, but they charge **
 $25** per car parking fee (so pack as many people in your car as you can).
  We recommend for the driver to purchase the lowest level annual membershi
 p which includes free parking. (Of course\, you may want a higher-level me
 mbership\, your choice.) **The parking fee can be applied to a membership 
 if you join the same day. It's nearly half of the $60 individual membershi
 p.** We walk at the Arboretum at least six times per year.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/313358020/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260214T190459Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260214T190459Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
