BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-appalachian-arts-crafts-rising-6th-8th-grade/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260615
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260616
DTSTAMP:20260604T003517
CREATED:20260127T202635Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260527T182536Z
UID:10006621-1781481600-1781567999@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Summer Art Camp | Appalachian Arts & Crafts (Rising 6th - 8th grade)
DESCRIPTION:REGISTER HERE \nBlending creativity with cultural heritage\, students will explore the artistic traditions of Appalachian culture through a series of hands-on crafts. They will begin the week creating vibrant painted barn quilts and learning basic weaving techniques with natural materials. They’ll spend the remainder of the week further developing their weaving skills to make reed baskets and needle felting a landscape.   \nMeet the Instructor: Kati Robbins\nKati Robbins has over 12 years of experience as an art educator\, teaching studio arts and crafts to a wide range of age groups in different learning environments. She is currently based in Asheville where she works as a high school art teacher. Her creative work focuses on mixed media and assemblage\, with a strong interest in collaborative and community based projects. She is inspired by Appalachian craft traditions\, natural materials and the surrounding landscape. When Kati isn’t teaching or making art\, she enjoys gardening\, cooking\, reading and hiking in the mountains. 
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-appalachian-arts-crafts-rising-6th-8th-grade/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Summer Art Camp
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/1976.62.71_New-1.jpg
GEO:35.5946714;-82.5512827
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Asheville Art Museum 2 South Pack Square Asheville NC 28801 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=2 South Pack Square:geo:-82.5512827,35.5946714
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-ancient-to-modern-mixed-media-traditions-reimagined-rising-6th-8th-grade/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260615
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260616
DTSTAMP:20260604T003517
CREATED:20260127T203717Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260527T182522Z
UID:10006616-1781481600-1781567999@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Summer Art Camp | Ancient to Modern: Mixed Media Traditions Reimagined (Rising 6th - 8th grade)
DESCRIPTION:REGISTER HERE \nThroughout history\, artists have experimented with wax\, fabric\, pigment\, metal\, and glass to create expressive and symbolic artworks. In this camp\, we’ll explore how ancient art-making techniques like batik\, encaustic\, and gilded mosaics can inspire new creative directions. Students will work hands-on with traditional materials and reinterpret them through a contemporary lens\, experimenting with resists\, mixed-media layering\, transparency\, and texture.  \nMeet the Instructor: Kristina Shriver\nKristina Shriver is a visual art educator with over 16 years of experience\, working with students of all ages. She teaches at Asheville High School and serves as an AP Studio Art Reader and mentor for other art educators. Kristina designs hands-on\, material-rich art experiences that connect historical techniques to contemporary practice\, emphasizing experimentation\, personal storytelling\, and meaningful creative exploration.   
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-ancient-to-modern-mixed-media-traditions-reimagined-rising-6th-8th-grade/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Summer Art Camp
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/2000.27.72.jpg
GEO:35.5946714;-82.5512827
