BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/a-musical-evening-with-decoda-ringdown-featuring-caroline-shaw-danni-lee-parpan/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260616T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260616T200000
DTSTAMP:20260604T003517
CREATED:20260317T221149Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260430T174251Z
UID:10006526-1781634600-1781640000@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:A Musical Evening with Decoda & Ringdown featuring Caroline Shaw & Danni Lee Parpan
DESCRIPTION:Decoda and Ringdown take the stage at the Asheville Art Museum for a vibrant\, genre-defying evening of music. This special collaboration brings together Decoda\, Carnegie Hall’s only affiliate ensemble\, with Ringdown for an electrifying evening of chamber music. Featuring celebrated songwriter Danni Lee Parpan and Pulitzer-Prize winning composer and North Carolina native Caroline Shaw\, Ringdown bridges classical and contemporary worlds together in a way that feels both expansive and deeply personal. \nThis program features celebrated works of chamber music\, alongside a collaborative set with Ringdown and Decoda\, blurring the lines between classical\, electronic\, and indie pop. Kicking off the 2026 Decoda Chamber Music Festival\, this concert experience is designed for devoted chamber music listeners and curious newcomers alike. \n————— \nRingdown’s music is like calling your first love on a rotary telephone\, percussively tearing out the hammers from a 1924 vintage upright\, and flinging each of them into space while you wait for every heartache you’ve ever felt to quietly return. Collaborators Caroline Shaw and Danni Lee Parpan—who between the two of them have a Pulitzer Prize\, a handful of Grammys\, and a “Best Drum Major Award”—describe Ringdown as an electronic cinematic pop duo based in Portland\, Oregon and New York City. Others have described Ringdown as the love child of Johannes Brahms and Brandi Carlile—if they were born in the same century and if Brahms was a queer woman. You decide. \nDecoda is an artist-led chamber music collective dedicated to creating a more compassionate and connected world through music. Decoda pairs virtuosic performance with deep community engagement\, bringing chamber music to concert halls\, schools\, shelters\, hospitals\, and correctional facilities. \nEach summer in the Asheville region\, Decoda leads the Decoda Chamber Music Festival\, a dynamic training program for young musicians who seek to develop both artistic excellence and social impact. Through side-by-side performances\, mentorship\, and creative collaboration\, participants explore how music can build community and inspire change. \nPurchase Tickets \n 
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/a-musical-evening-with-decoda-ringdown-featuring-caroline-shaw-danni-lee-parpan/
CATEGORIES:Performance
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/Decoda-Ringdown_split.png
END:VEVENT
