BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-art-around-the-world-rising-3rd-5th-grade/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260622
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260623
DTSTAMP:20260604T003517
CREATED:20260127T204224Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260527T182511Z
UID:10006626-1782086400-1782172799@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Summer Art Camp | Art Around the World (Rising 3rd – 5th grade)
DESCRIPTION:JOIN THE WAITLIST \nStudents will investigate artists and artworks from each continent using a variety of processes and materials. They will explore drawing\, painting\, printmaking\, sculpture and collage. During art camp\, students will collect artworks to create a portfolio that crosses all continents and cultures from around the world.     \nMeet the Instructor: Sarah Medsker\nSarah Medsker has a master’s degree in education and is an art teacher in western North Carolina\, having taught students between kindergarten and 8th grade. Teaching children is her passion\, as she has been facilitating art-making for over 15 years. When she is not teaching art\, she loves traveling\, cooking\, reading and exploring professional development opportunities in the field of art education.  
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-art-around-the-world-rising-3rd-5th-grade/
CATEGORIES:Summer Art Camp
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/1981.17.114.61.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-art-around-the-world-rising-3rd-5th-grade-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260622
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260623
DTSTAMP:20260604T003517
CREATED:20260127T204521Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260527T182456Z
UID:10006631-1782086400-1782172799@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Summer Art Camp | Paper and Book Making (Rising 3rd – 5th grade)
DESCRIPTION:JOIN THE WAITLIST \n The first two days of this camp will be about tearing up\, mashing\, blending and laying out paper to dry into curated sheets – cut and folded into books we will make on the following three days.  There are so many ways to make a book! Picture journals with ribbons\, folded snake books and bedazzled covers!  \nMeet the Instructor: Maggie Imhoff\nMaggie Imhoff is an educator of twenty-three years\, including\, most recently\, the Art teacher at Ira B Jones elementary school in Asheville\, NC. She has taught at several summer camps\, created outdoor art experiences for kids as well as directed at a children’s circus. She loves to celebrate art in her everyday life. She knits\, paints\, sings\, and dances.  This quote from Phylicia Rashad sums it up: “Before a child speaks\, it sings.  Before they write\, they paint. As soon as they stand\, they dance. Art is the basis of human expression.” As an art educator\, it brings her joy to bring art to children’s lives.   
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-art-around-the-world-rising-3rd-5th-grade-2/
CATEGORIES:Summer Art Camp
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/2012.03.38.jpg
END:VEVENT
