BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-the-joy-of-painting-rising-k-2nd-grade/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260629
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260630
DTSTAMP:20260604T003517
CREATED:20260127T204811Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260527T182444Z
UID:10006636-1782691200-1782777599@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Summer Art Camp | The Joy of Painting! (Rising K - 2nd grade)
DESCRIPTION:JOIN THE WAITLIST \n In this camp\, participants will explore different paint mediums and techniques.  We will work with watercolor\, acrylics and tempera (all washable).  We will learn about brush techniques\, finger painting\, wax resist and printing to name just a few.  The color wheel\, warm and cool colors plus complementary colors will be discussed and an avenue to explore. Your child will get lost in the engaging and colorful world of paint!  \nMeet the Instructor: Maggie Imhoff\nMaggie Imhoff is an educator of twenty-three years\, including\, most recently\, the Art teacher at Ira B Jones elementary school in Asheville\, NC. She has taught at several summer camps\, created outdoor art experiences for kids as well as directed at a children’s circus. She loves to celebrate art in her everyday life. She knits\, paints\, sings\, and dances.  This quote from Phylicia Rashad sums it up: “Before a child speaks\, it sings.  Before they write\, they paint. As soon as they stand\, they dance. Art is the basis of human expression.” As an art educator\, it brings her joy to bring art to children’s lives. 
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-the-joy-of-painting-rising-k-2nd-grade/
CATEGORIES:Summer Art Camp
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/2008.25.02.24-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/summer-art-camp-storybook-art-rising-k-2nd-grade/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260629
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260630
