SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260604T043526Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260802T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260802T160000
SUMMARY:Walk at Little Champion Plant in Waynesville on National Ice Cream
  Sandwich Day
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nOld Timers call this prop
 erty on Old Howell Mill Road near Old Asheville Highway "Little Champion" 
 because the Canton Champion Paper Mill put in this plant to put wax on pap
 er for making milk cartons. The Mill changed hands several times\, but the
  Old Timers kept calling it Little Champion. (Note that Google Maps calls 
 it Evergreen Packaging\, and the sign on the building now says Suzano.)\n\
 nThe 3/4-mile walking track at Little Champion runs by Richland Creek with
  lots of creekside trees\, by fishing spots\, and by a picnic area. There 
 is a bathroom in the middle of the track. We plan to do 4 counterclockwise
  laps. (Yes\, you are free to do fewer or even more!) That will make a tot
 al of 5 KM/3.1 miles.\n\nBe sure you enter the property on the Old Ashevil
 le Highway (east) side of the plant (the side with the Suzano sign) on Ken
  Thompson Drive\, go to the rear of the building\, and then turning left\,
  go ***all the way to the far end of the back of the parking lot\, down by
  the sign designating the Drop Lot***. It is in that corner of the parking
  lot where we will assemble. (If you go down the stairs into the middle of
  the track\, you will be in the wrong place and will miss where the group 
 is assembling.)\n\nDress appropriately for the weather\; consider a hat an
 d sunscreen. There is a little hill on each lap\, so some may want walking
  sticks. Bring **plenty of water** and a protein snack. This is a paved tr
 ack\, so tennis shoes will be fine. Dogs are welcome. Strollers will have 
 no problem.\n\nSince it is National Ice Cream Sandwich Day\, at the end of
  the walk we will have available free ice cream sandwiches for our walkers
 . Now\, how's that for a hot summer afternoon!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/315003401/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260528T231928Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260528T231928Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
